14:21.835 --> 14:23.168
Hair of the dog.

14:23.170 --> 14:24.219
Oh.

14:24.221 --> 14:27.923
Oh, that one's not dog.

14:27.925 --> 14:29.674
Bye! Call me!

14:29.676 --> 14:30.725
Oh.

14:30.727 --> 14:31.893
I will!

14:31.895 --> 14:35.096
As soon as I remember your name.

14:36.415 --> 14:37.432
Who was that?

14:37.434 --> 14:38.633
Oh, I just tapped

14:38.635 --> 14:40.769
a little strange last night.

14:40.771 --> 14:41.736
(dog barks)

14:41.738 --> 14:43.572
Which one did you tap?

14:45.975 --> 14:47.442
I'll give you a hint.

14:47.444 --> 14:49.694
I didn't do the dog
people style.

14:53.332 --> 14:57.452
It's walking like Zippy, but it
sure ain't talking like Zippy.

14:57.454 --> 14:59.704
Yeah. I don't know him
as well as you do.

14:59.706 --> 15:01.322
Is he prone to having
mental breakdowns?

15:01.324 --> 15:02.340
Prone, no.

15:02.342 --> 15:05.493
Eligible, certainly.

15:05.495 --> 15:08.496
♪ Men. ♪

15:08.498 --> 15:10.181
Whoa, look who's getting busy.

15:10.183 --> 15:11.666
Hey.

15:11.668 --> 15:14.436
Mr. Harper,
we were just making out.

15:14.438 --> 15:16.354
Yeah, we all know
what happens after making out.

15:16.356 --> 15:17.722
Making in and out.

15:19.725 --> 15:21.943
(clears throat)

15:24.030 --> 15:25.680
Listen up,
grasshoppers.

15:25.682 --> 15:29.651
You know how they say that
marijuana leads to harder drugs?

15:29.653 --> 15:32.070
Well, the same thing
applies to the human tongue.

15:32.072 --> 15:33.822
It leads to
harder organs.

15:35.791 --> 15:38.192
Now, if you are not careful,
you're gonna wake up one morning

15:38.194 --> 15:39.828
with a big-headed
bun in the oven.

15:40.997 --> 15:42.247
No offense, Charlie Brown.

15:42.249 --> 15:45.917
I'm begging you,
please leave.

15:45.919 --> 15:48.336
Relax, I'm just
looking out for you.

15:48.338 --> 15:49.804
Here, tell you what.

15:49.806 --> 15:52.924
Take the young lady out
for a nice dinner, on me.

15:52.926 --> 15:55.644
It's a dollar.

15:55.646 --> 15:57.395
You're welcome!

15:59.515 --> 16:01.683
♪ Men. ♪

16:01.685 --> 16:04.569
I think we have a problem.

16:04.571 --> 16:06.237
Your father?

16:06.239 --> 16:07.272
Yeah.

16:07.274 --> 16:09.107
He's acting like
my Uncle Charlie.

16:09.109 --> 16:11.409
I mean, he's even dressing
like my Uncle Charlie.

16:11.411 --> 16:15.664
The only thing left of my dad
is his cheapness.

16:18.200 --> 16:21.836
Well, Jake,
he suffered a big loss.

16:23.205 --> 16:26.007
People deal with that
in different ways.

16:26.009 --> 16:28.076
I mean, I still haven't
processed the grief

16:28.078 --> 16:30.628
over my marriage
ending.

16:30.630 --> 16:34.799
I'm... sure someday it'll hit me

16:34.801 --> 16:39.587
that the most important person
in my life is gone.

16:41.924 --> 16:44.526
My soul mate.

16:44.528 --> 16:46.895
My best friend.

16:46.897 --> 16:48.446
My lover.

16:50.366 --> 16:53.368
In the meantime,
you just carry on.

16:54.603 --> 16:58.907
And you to try to fill that void
by having casual drunk sex

16:58.909 --> 17:00.909
with strange, hot women
that don't mind

17:00.911 --> 17:03.128
if you dance around
in their panties.

17:07.333 --> 17:11.586
Is everybody turning into
Uncle Charlie?

17:11.588 --> 17:13.805
♪ Men. ♪

17:15.290 --> 17:17.842
Ah, Cuban in one hand,

17:17.844 --> 17:19.260
scotch in the other.

17:19.262 --> 17:21.596
All I need is
a French chick in my lap

17:21.598 --> 17:23.732
and I'm the
United-freakin'-Nations.

17:23.734 --> 17:25.734
(knocking)

17:25.736 --> 17:27.435
Got a minute?

17:27.437 --> 17:29.654
Uh, pretty busy, but okay.

17:29.656 --> 17:32.824
Thanks.

17:32.826 --> 17:34.526
All right, look...

17:36.979 --> 17:38.646
People are really
worried about you.

17:38.648 --> 17:41.950
Hey, the only reason people
are worried about me is 'cause

17:41.952 --> 17:45.420
they can't wrap their heads
around how cool I am.

17:45.422 --> 17:48.840
Yeah, no, I don't
think that's it.

17:49.759 --> 17:52.043
Look, I know you
miss your brother.

17:52.045 --> 17:53.128
(scoffs)

17:53.130 --> 17:54.429
Miss my brother?

17:54.431 --> 17:55.496
That parasitic leech.

17:55.498 --> 17:56.714
Not likely.

17:56.716 --> 18:00.385
Hey, you remember that
shrink that you sent me to?

18:01.103 --> 18:02.270
Maybe you should
go see her.

18:02.272 --> 18:03.471
What for? I'm fine.

18:03.473 --> 18:04.889
What's your name?

18:04.891 --> 18:05.840
Charlie Harper.

18:05.842 --> 18:07.192
You're not fine.

18:07.194 --> 18:10.645
Well, I guess we'll have
to agree to disagree.

18:12.481 --> 18:15.617
Okay.

18:15.619 --> 18:18.570
I'll tell you what, why
don't you get some rest,

18:18.572 --> 18:21.990
maybe lick your finger,
stick it in a light socket,

18:21.992 --> 18:25.710
and we'll revisit
this in the morning.

18:25.712 --> 18:27.662
You got it, big fella.

18:31.967 --> 18:34.135
Who the hell was that?

18:36.806 --> 18:38.306
♪ Men. ♪

18:38.308 --> 18:42.594
♪ It's got oats
and corn and wheat ♪

18:42.596 --> 18:46.481
♪ It's the sweetest
breakfast treat ♪

18:46.483 --> 18:47.548
♪ It's... ♪

18:47.550 --> 18:51.385
♪ Maple, maple,
maaaaple-icious! ♪

18:53.022 --> 18:55.406
Uh, what are you
doing in here?

18:55.408 --> 18:57.358
What are you
doing in here?

18:57.360 --> 18:59.611
It's my shower!

18:59.613 --> 19:02.230
Once again, agree
to disagree.

19:02.232 --> 19:03.198
Okay, listen...

19:03.200 --> 19:04.899
Whoa! Nice penis!

19:04.901 --> 19:06.901
You could paint a
face on that thing

19:06.903 --> 19:09.170
and ride in the
car pool lane.

19:12.842 --> 19:14.425
Thank you.

19:14.427 --> 19:16.711
Uh-oh, what's going
on down there?

19:16.713 --> 19:19.931
Call the cops;
I've been robbed!

19:19.933 --> 19:21.683
♪ Men. ♪

19:23.052 --> 19:24.519
ALAN:
&lt;i>Great idea.&lt;/i>

19:24.521 --> 19:26.087
You and me, Vegas.

19:26.089 --> 19:27.088
(chuckles)

19:27.090 --> 19:28.640
Yep.

19:28.642 --> 19:30.591
I am gonna show you a good time.

19:30.593 --> 19:32.277
They love me in Vegas.

19:32.279 --> 19:33.728
I'm sure they do.

19:33.730 --> 19:37.282
Trust me, the name Charlie
Harper opens a lot of doors.

19:37.284 --> 19:39.484
And a lot of legs.

19:39.486 --> 19:40.952
No kidding.

19:40.954 --> 19:42.737
But be sure to wear a condom.

19:42.739 --> 19:45.540
Not everything stays in Vegas.

19:45.542 --> 19:47.608
Okay.

19:47.610 --> 19:49.494
Well, here we are.

19:49.496 --> 19:51.663
Really? This doesn't
look like the Bellagio.

19:51.665 --> 19:53.498
It's the, uh, back entrance.

19:53.500 --> 19:56.617
Ah, not the only back entrance
we'll be using this weekend.

19:56.619 --> 19:58.503
Am I right? Up top.

20:00.756 --> 20:02.840
(laughs)

20:02.842 --> 20:04.008
Hello, Mr. Harper.

20:04.010 --> 20:05.727
If you could just
come with us.

20:05.729 --> 20:07.061
Uh, don't forget my bags.

20:07.063 --> 20:08.763
We'll be going to
the presidential suite.

20:08.765 --> 20:11.316
Oh, yes, sir.

20:11.318 --> 20:12.734
Slip 'em both a sawbuck.

20:12.736 --> 20:14.235
I'll see you in the room.

20:14.237 --> 20:15.770
Will do.

20:15.772 --> 20:17.405
(tires screeching)

20:19.241 --> 20:20.909
This way, Mr. Harper.

20:22.745 --> 20:24.162
So who's playing the big room?

20:24.164 --> 20:25.747
Celine? Elton?

20:25.749 --> 20:27.999
I'm gonna want tickets-- comped.

20:28.001 --> 20:30.418
♪ Men. ♪

20:30.553 --> 20:31.687
♪ Men. ♪

20:31.689 --> 20:33.522
Hello, concierge? Yes.

20:33.524 --> 20:35.858
Um, this is Charlie Harper
in the presidential suite.

20:35.860 --> 20:38.393
Uh, I'm gonna need
a bucket of ice,

20:38.395 --> 20:41.647
a bottle of scotch
and two Asian hookers.

20:43.733 --> 20:45.450
You know what, they're small.

20:45.487 --> 20:47.955
Make it three.

20:47.956 --> 20:49.790
Yes, thanks.

20:49.791 --> 20:51.292
(sighs)

20:52.974 --> 20:55.209
Winning.

20:55.210 --> 20:59.210
